{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** The values of **exactly two** nodes of a binary search tree were swapped by mistake. Put them back without changing the tree's structure (swap the values in place; return nothing)."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/e87371d1-c011-4799-9a1e-b0ce40d30be8.svg",
      "alt": "The tree 3, 1, 4, null, null, 2 where 2 and 3 were swapped. Its in-order list is 1, 3, 2, 4: one drop, from 3 to 2. The first wrong node is the bigger value at the start of a drop, 3, and the second is the smaller value at the end of the last drop, 2. Swapping them back gives 1, 2, 3, 4.",
      "width": 671,
      "height": 414,
