    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "root = [1, 3, null, null, 2]   ->  [3, 1, null, null, 2]   (1 and 3 were swapped)\nroot = [3, 1, 4, null, null, 2]   ->  [2, 1, 4, null, null, 3]   (2 and 3 were swapped)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The idea"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A BST's in-order walk is increasing. Swapping two values creates either **one drop** (if they were neighbours in sorted order, like 1 3 2 4) or **two drops** (like 1 **5** 3 4 **2** 6: drops at 5→3 and 4→2). In both cases, the first wrong value is the **bigger** side of the **first** drop, and the second wrong value is the **smaller** side of the **last** drop."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Sort the values and write them back"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Collect the values in-order, sort them, and overwrite the nodes in in-order again. It fixes any number of misplaced values, not just two."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function recoverTree(root) {\n  const nodes = [];\n  const inorder = (node) => {\n    if (node === null) return;\n    inorder(node.left);\n    nodes.push(node);\n    inorder(node.right);\n  };\n  inorder(root);\n  const sorted = nodes.map((n) => n.val).sort((a, b) => a - b);\n  nodes.forEach((n, i) => { n.val = sorted[i]; });     // in-order position i gets the i-th smallest\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def recover_tree(root):\n    nodes = []\n\n    def inorder(node):\n        if node is None:\n            return\n        inorder(node.left)\n        nodes.append(node)\n        inorder(node.right)\n\n    inorder(root)\n    values = sorted(n.val for n in nodes)\n    for n, v in zip(nodes, values):\n        n.val = v                         # in-order position i gets the i-th smallest"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "void recoverTree(TreeNode root) {\n    List<TreeNode> nodes = new ArrayList<>();\n    inorder(root, nodes);\n    int[] values = new int[nodes.size()];\n    for (int i = 0; i < values.length; i++) values[i] = nodes.get(i).val;\n    Arrays.sort(values);\n    for (int i = 0; i < values.length; i++) nodes.get(i).val = values[i];   // the i-th smallest\n}\n\nvoid inorder(TreeNode node, List<TreeNode> nodes) {\n    if (node == null) return;\n    inorder(node.left, nodes);\n    nodes.add(node);\n    inorder(node.right, nodes);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "void inorder(TreeNode* node, vector<TreeNode*>& nodes) {\n    if (node == nullptr) return;\n    inorder(node->left, nodes);\n    nodes.push_back(node);\n    inorder(node->right, nodes);\n}\n\nvoid recoverTree(TreeNode* root) {\n    vector<TreeNode*> nodes;\n    inorder(root, nodes);\n    vector<int> values;\n    for (TreeNode* n : nodes) values.push_back(n->val);\n    sort(values.begin(), values.end());\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < nodes.size(); i++) nodes[i]->val = values[i];   // the i-th smallest\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n log n), space O(n).**"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. In-order with a previous pointer"
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "recover-bst",
      "caption": "Compare each in-order node with the previous one; a drop marks a swapped node."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function recoverTree(root) {\n  let prev = null, first = null, second = null;\n  const inorder = (node) => {\n    if (node === null) return;\n    inorder(node.left);\n    if (prev !== null && prev.val > node.val) {   // a drop\n      if (first === null) first = prev;           // bigger side of the first drop\n      second = node;                              // smaller side of the latest drop\n    }\n    prev = node;\n    inorder(node.right);\n  };\n  inorder(root);\n  [first.val, second.val] = [second.val, first.val];\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def recover_tree(root):\n    prev = first = second = None\n\n    def inorder(node):\n        nonlocal prev, first, second\n        if node is None:\n            return\n        inorder(node.left)\n        if prev is not None and prev.val > node.val:   # a drop\n            if first is None:\n                first = prev                      # bigger side of the first drop\n            second = node                         # smaller side of the latest drop\n        prev = node\n        inorder(node.right)\n\n    inorder(root)\n    first.val, second.val = second.val, first.val"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "TreeNode prev, first, second;\n\nvoid recoverTree(TreeNode root) {\n    prev = first = second = null;\n    inorder(root);\n    int t = first.val;\n    first.val = second.val;\n    second.val = t;\n}\n\nvoid inorder(TreeNode node) {\n    if (node == null) return;\n    inorder(node.left);\n    if (prev != null && prev.val > node.val) {       // a drop\n        if (first == null) first = prev;             // bigger side of the first drop\n        second = node;                               // smaller side of the latest drop\n    }\n    prev = node;\n    inorder(node.right);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "void inorder(TreeNode* node, TreeNode*& prev, TreeNode*& first, TreeNode*& second) {\n    if (node == nullptr) return;\n    inorder(node->left, prev, first, second);\n    if (prev != nullptr && prev->val > node->val) {  // a drop\n        if (first == nullptr) first = prev;          // bigger side of the first drop\n        second = node;                               // smaller side of the latest drop\n    }\n    prev = node;\n    inorder(node->right, prev, first, second);\n}\n\nvoid recoverTree(TreeNode* root) {\n    TreeNode *prev = nullptr, *first = nullptr, *second = nullptr;\n    inorder(root, prev, first, second);\n    swap(first->val, second->val);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(h)** for the recursion."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "3. Morris traversal: O(1) space"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The follow-up asks for constant space. **Morris traversal** walks in-order without a stack: before going left, it makes the rightmost node of the left subtree point back to the current node (a temporary \"thread\"), and removes the thread the second time it arrives. The drop check is the same as approach 2."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function recoverTree(root) {\n  let prev = null, first = null, second = null;\n  const visit = (node) => {\n    if (prev !== null && prev.val > node.val) {\n      if (first === null) first = prev;\n      second = node;\n    }\n    prev = node;\n  };\n  let node = root;\n  while (node !== null) {\n    if (node.left === null) {\n      visit(node);\n      node = node.right;\n      continue;\n    }\n    let pred = node.left;                  // rightmost node of the left subtree\n    while (pred.right !== null && pred.right !== node) pred = pred.right;\n    if (pred.right === null) {\n      pred.right = node;                   // thread back, then go left\n      node = node.left;\n    } else {\n      pred.right = null;                   // second arrival: remove the thread\n      visit(node);\n      node = node.right;\n    }\n  }\n  [first.val, second.val] = [second.val, first.val];\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def recover_tree(root):\n    prev = first = second = None\n    node = root\n    while node is not None:\n        if node.left is not None:\n            pred = node.left              # rightmost node of the left subtree\n            while pred.right is not None and pred.right is not node:\n                pred = pred.right\n            if pred.right is None:\n                pred.right = node         # thread back, then go left\n                node = node.left\n                continue\n            pred.right = None             # second arrival: remove the thread\n        if prev is not None and prev.val > node.val:\n            if first is None:\n                first = prev\n            second = node\n        prev = node\n        node = node.right\n    first.val, second.val = second.val, first.val"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "void recoverTree(TreeNode root) {\n    TreeNode prev = null, first = null, second = null, node = root;\n    while (node != null) {\n        if (node.left != null) {\n            TreeNode pred = node.left;                   // rightmost node of the left subtree\n            while (pred.right != null && pred.right != node) pred = pred.right;\n            if (pred.right == null) {\n                pred.right = node;                       // thread back, then go left\n                node = node.left;\n                continue;\n            }\n            pred.right = null;                           // second arrival: remove the thread\n        }\n        if (prev != null && prev.val > node.val) {\n            if (first == null) first = prev;\n            second = node;\n        }\n        prev = node;\n        node = node.right;\n    }\n    int t = first.val;\n    first.val = second.val;\n    second.val = t;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "void recoverTree(TreeNode* root) {\n    TreeNode *prev = nullptr, *first = nullptr, *second = nullptr, *node = root;\n    while (node != nullptr) {\n        if (node->left != nullptr) {\n            TreeNode* pred = node->left;                 // rightmost node of the left subtree\n            while (pred->right != nullptr && pred->right != node) pred = pred->right;\n            if (pred->right == nullptr) {\n                pred->right = node;                      // thread back, then go left\n                node = node->left;\n                continue;\n            }\n            pred->right = nullptr;                       // second arrival: remove the thread\n        }\n        if (prev != nullptr && prev->val > node->val) {\n            if (first == nullptr) first = prev;\n            second = node;\n        }\n        prev = node;\n        node = node->right;\n    }\n    swap(first->val, second->val);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(1).** Each edge is walked at most a few times, and every thread is removed, so the tree ends up exactly as it started — apart from the fixed values."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "Sort the values and write them back",
          "time": "O(n log n)",
          "timeWhy": "Collect **n** values and **sort** them, then write them back in order.",
          "space": "O(n)",
          "spaceWhy": "The **list of values**."
        },
        {
          "approach": "In-order with a previous pointer",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "One in-order pass spots the **two out-of-order nodes**.",
          "space": "O(h)",
          "spaceWhy": "The recursion **as deep as the tree**."
        },
        {
          "approach": "Morris traversal",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "Each edge is walked **a few times** while threading predecessors.",
          "space": "O(1)",
          "spaceWhy": "It borrows **empty right pointers** and removes every thread again."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Adjacent values swapped** — only one drop; first and second come from the same drop.",
        "**The root is one of the swapped nodes.**",
        "**Two nodes total** — the drop is between them.",
        "**Far-apart values** — two drops; take the first's bigger side and the last's smaller side."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
